Do not assume an agent is merely a stat sheet.

Model each player as a dynamic policy:

PlayerAgent = {
    morphology,
    athletic capabilities,
    skill distributions,
    learned techniques,
    decision policy,
    perception model,
    reaction latency,
    risk tolerance,
    fatigue response,
    injury susceptibility,
    confidence state,
    opponent models,
    teammate models,
    coach relationship,
    historical experience,
    adaptation rate,
    uncertainty
}

Behavior should emerge from the interaction between these variables rather than from fixed animations.

